      "hints": [
        "Substitute $x = 4$ into $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{8}{x^2} - \\frac{10}{(2x-3)^2}$ to find the tangent slope.",
        "Find the perpendicular normal gradient $m_{\\text{norm}} = -\\frac{1}{m_{\\text{tan}}}$.",
        "Write the equation of the normal in $y = mx + c$ form through $P(4, 3)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate the derivative at $x = 4$ to find the tangent slope:\n$$m_{\\text{tan}} = \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=4} = \\frac{8}{4^2} - \\frac{10}{(2(4) - 3)^2} = \\frac{8}{16} - \\frac{10}{25} = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{1}{10}$$",
        "Find the perpendicular normal gradient:\n$$m_{\\text{norm}} = -\\frac{1}{m_{\\text{tan}}} = -10$$",
        "Write the equation of the normal line through $P(4, 3)$:\n$$y - 3 = -10(x - 4) \\implies y - 3 = -10x + 40 \\implies y = -10x + 43$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
