      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 8x^{-2} - 10(2x-3)^{-2}$ with respect to $x$ to find $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.",
        "Substitute $x = 4$ to find the numerical rate of change."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 8x^{-2} - 10(2x - 3)^{-2}$ with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 8(-2)x^{-3} - 10(-2)(2x - 3)^{-3}(2) = -16x^{-3} + 40(2x - 3)^{-3} = -\\frac{16}{x^3} + \\frac{40}{(2x - 3)^3}$$",
        "Substitute $x = 4$ into the second derivative:\n$$\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=4} = -\\frac{16}{4^3} + \\frac{40}{(2(4) - 3)^3} = -\\frac{16}{64} + \\frac{40}{125} = -\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{8}{25}$$",
        "Simplify the fractional evaluation:\n$$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = -\\frac{25}{100} + \\frac{32}{100} = \\frac{7}{100} = 0.07$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
