      "hints": [
        "Integrate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ term by term, including constant $+ c$.",
        "Substitute $P(4, 3)$ to determine $c$.",
        "Substitute $x = -1$ into the curve equation to find $q$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 8x^{-2} - 10(2x - 3)^{-2}$ with respect to $x$:\n$$y = \\int [8x^{-2} - 10(2x - 3)^{-2}]\\,dx = \\frac{8x^{-1}}{-1} - 10\\left[\\frac{(2x - 3)^{-1}}{(-1) \\cdot 2}\\right] + c = -\\frac{8}{x} + \\frac{5}{2x - 3} + c$$",
        "Substitute $P(4, 3)$ to find the integration constant $c$:\n$$3 = -\\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{5}{2(4) - 3} + c = -2 + \\frac{5}{5} + c = -2 + 1 + c = -1 + c \\implies c = 4$$",
        "Write the complete curve equation:\n$$y = -\\frac{8}{x} + \\frac{5}{2x - 3} + 4$$",
        "Substitute $x = -1$ to find $q$:\n$$q = -\\frac{8}{-1} + \\frac{5}{2(-1) - 3} + 4 = 8 + \\frac{5}{-5} + 4 = 8 - 1 + 4 = 11$$"
      ],
